  "gr-u4-1": {
    "file": "gr-u4-1.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We can use comparative adjectives to compare two people or things.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "cb208e8f687f681a"
  },
  "gr-u4-2": {
    "file": "gr-u4-2.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "Tom is taller than Mary.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "fd6b54064b835d9f"
  },
  "gr-u12-1": {
    "file": "gr-u12-1.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We use superlative adjectives to compare three or more people or things.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "00b3ba12fabdafb3"
  },
  "gr-u12-2": {
    "file": "gr-u12-2.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "Tom is the tallest in his class.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "a19ffc8f7dd6177c"
  },
  "gr-u12-3": {
    "file": "gr-u12-3.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "This is the biggest of the three bags.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "bd12e3b9aab6ed43"
  },
  "gr-a1": {
    "file": "gr-a1.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "There are two kinds of articles in English: the indefinite article (a / an) and the definite article (the).",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "58665ef8ee77ba48"
  },
  "gr-a2": {
    "file": "gr-a2.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We use a / an",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "3cb6ccd1fa811699"
  },
  "gr-a3": {
    "file": "gr-a3.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "with singular countable nouns when we are talking about them in general.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "f5b25bc87c53e3df"
  },
  "gr-a4": {
    "file": "gr-a4.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "An ant is a tiny animal.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "c235cd5a14ce87e8"
  },
  "gr-a5": {
    "file": "gr-a5.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "after the verbs to be and to have.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "eb07bcf45e113e74"
  },
  "gr-a6": {
    "file": "gr-a6.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "I'm a student.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "8ed976bd1dd8c8f8"
  },
  "gr-a7": {
    "file": "gr-a7.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "I have an eraser.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "29b11f454b827497"
  },
  "gr-a8": {
    "file": "gr-a8.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We use the",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "2d06fb9eee1048cf"
  },
  "gr-a9": {
    "file": "gr-a9.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "with singular or plural nouns when we already know them or when they are mentioned for the second time.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "9d5df93a08b1eded"
  },
  "gr-a10": {
    "file": "gr-a10.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "The bike in front of her house is nice.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "7ebacdd1e276fe50"
  },
  "gr-a11": {
    "file": "gr-a11.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "with nouns which are unique.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "3b5052b51b9c4bf0"
  },
  "gr-a12": {
    "file": "gr-a12.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "The air is dirty.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "0cc140fc6e9b5560"
  },
  "gr-f1": {
    "file": "gr-f1.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We use the future simple to talk about an action that happens in the future.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "e5e2ec618df1b2fa"
  },
  "gr-f2": {
    "file": "gr-f2.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "My father will travel on the Moon in a super car in the future.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "4890e4e7a53483f8"
  },
  "gr-f3": {
    "file": "gr-f3.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We'll live in that cottage next year.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "f11a5dd3bcba601a"
  },
  "gr-f4": {
    "file": "gr-f4.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We won't live in that cottage anytime soon.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "8fe17dad40d95bfa"
  },
  "gr-f5": {
    "file": "gr-f5.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "Will they live on the Moon?",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "1a5a2e762ffc1f49"
  },
  "gr-f6": {
    "file": "gr-f6.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "Yes, they will.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "e3334f30f11b3a3e"
  },
  "gr-f7": {
    "file": "gr-f7.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "No, they won't.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "974acfd67d89b75b"
  },
  "gr-m1": {
    "file": "gr-m1.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We use might + V to talk about actions that are possible in the future (we are not sure if they will happen or not).",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "7cd05cdd3c2d403e"
  },
  "gr-m2": {
    "file": "gr-m2.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We might live in a UFO.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "9f84c7ed9480ae8d"
  },
  "gr-m3": {
    "file": "gr-m3.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "They might not travel in cars.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "0f451dc43ea473e9"
  },
  "gr-c1": {
    "file": "gr-c1.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
